WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.820
Lesson eight, the honest test.

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:09.166
A hundred tracks the walker has never seen, full episodes, and the unmodified reward.

00:00:09.766 --> 00:00:15.283
The champion averages two hundred and sixty four points, give or take sixty seven.

00:00:15.283 --> 00:00:20.855
It falls on eleven of a hundred tracks, and reaches the finish on eighty nine.

00:00:21.455 --> 00:00:23.009
So it's not solved.

00:00:23.009 --> 00:00:27.153
Three hundred is the bar, and none of a hundred runs reached it.

00:00:27.153 --> 00:00:32.517
But look at how consistent it is: almost every track lands close to the average.

00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:34.906
Where do the points go?

00:00:34.906 --> 00:00:38.715
Walking to the finish earns about three hundred and sixty.

00:00:38.715 --> 00:00:45.825
On average, this walker earns three hundred and fifty one from moving, and spends seventy six on motor effort.

00:00:46.425 --> 00:00:49.458
So the limit isn't falling, and it isn't speed.

00:00:49.458 --> 00:00:50.561
It's effort.

00:00:50.561 --> 00:00:53.539
The network pushes its motors almost flat out.

00:00:53.539 --> 00:00:58.141
To score higher, it would have to walk as far while working less hard.

00:00:58.741 --> 00:01:02.024
Now the same hundred tracks for my NEAT walker.

00:01:02.024 --> 00:01:04.711
NEAT averages one hundred and eighty.

00:01:04.711 --> 00:01:07.576
CMA-ES averages two hundred and seventy.

00:01:07.576 --> 00:01:14.323
The difference is ninety one points, and CMA-ES scores higher on ninety three of the hundred tracks.

00:01:14.923 --> 00:01:18.467
It also falls far less: seven falls against ten.

00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:25.411
A fixed network with the right size, plus covariance learning, beat evolving the network's shape.

00:01:26.011 --> 00:01:29.019
How does it compare with gradient methods?

00:01:29.019 --> 00:01:31.907
PPO reached two hundred and seventy two.

00:01:31.907 --> 00:01:36.238
TD3 reached about three hundred and ten, in only two hours.

00:01:36.838 --> 00:01:42.420
CMA-ES used far more simulation steps: about one hundred and eighteen million.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:52.002
But it needed no gradients, no critic and no replay buffer, and its whole policy is about a hundred and forty times smaller than TD3's.

00:01:52.602 --> 00:02:05.519
That's the whole story: a task, a network of nine hundred and thirty two numbers, an algorithm that only ranks whole episodes, and a fitness that leads it, one small step at a time, to walking.
